From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sckiyo <sckiyo@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:26:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: rockchip: rockchip_sai: keep 32-bit slots in clock
 provider mode

Commit 8a6391ec6693 ("ASoC: rockchip: rockchip_sai: Set slot width for
non-TDM mode") sets the slot width to the sample width.
Backported to 6.18.y as 131e01ba249f.
For S16_LE, the SAI then sends 32fs frames.
The RK3576 HDMI TX takes I2S from SAI6 and needs 64fs frames.
S16_LE HDMI audio is silent. S32_LE HDMI audio plays.

Keep 32-bit slots when the SAI provides the clocks.
Use the sample width only when the codec provides the clocks.
Codec-clock configurations keep the upstream behavior.

Fixes: 8a6391ec6693 ("ASoC: rockchip: rockchip_sai: Set slot width for non-TDM mode")
Signed-off-by: sckiyo <sckiyo@outlook.com>
---
 sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
index b38c2cb..6355b66 100644
--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_sai.c
@@ -628,9 +628,12 @@ static int rockchip_sai_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 
 	regmap_update_bits(sai->regmap, reg, SAI_XCR_VDW_MASK | SAI_XCR_CSR_MASK, val);
 
-	if (!sai->is_tdm)
+	if (!sai->is_tdm) {
+		/* The HDMI TX I2S input on SAI6 needs 64fs frames. */
+		slot_width = sai->is_master_mode ? 32 : params_physical_width(params);
 		regmap_update_bits(sai->regmap, reg, SAI_XCR_SBW_MASK,
-				   SAI_XCR_SBW(params_physical_width(params)));
+				   SAI_XCR_SBW(slot_width));
+	}
 
 	regmap_read(sai->regmap, reg, &val);
 
